 -- JoySort Release Bot <release@joysort.cc>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:41:07 +0000

omp-web (0.5.22) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Fix host→web stream corruption and permanent RPC decoder hang that
    stalled session routes (closes #96). The session-host transport's
    onDrain credited dropped bytes as delivered: Bun UDS socket.write
    drops the unaccepted tail, so a large frame meeting a full socket
    buffer lost its remainder and corrupted the stream. Drain now
    rewrites from the queue entry's offset; multi-MiB frames deliver
    byte-exact under backpressure.
  * The web RPC decoder self-heals: the SDK RpcFrameDecoder never clears
    its pending chunk sequence on throw, so one interrupted sequence
    poisoned every later frame and get_state/get_entries/get_tree
    responses were dropped forever. The wrapper now resets the decoder
    and retries once (recovering the interrupting response intact), and
    throttles the decode-error log to 1/s.
  * Read-only host queries (get_*) are bounded at 30 s: a lost response
    fails retryable instead of hanging the route indefinitely; the
    client's reconcile poll retries.

