 -- JoySort Release Bot <release@joysort.cc>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 02:45:21 +0000

omp-web (0.5.8) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Plan-mode transition failures no longer discard the composer
    (issue #68 follow-up). A fleet remote still on omp-web 0.5.6 has no
    `set_plan_mode` command and answers HTTP 500 through the machine
    proxy; the `/plan` builtin treated that failure as a handled
    success, so the optimistic input clear silently dropped the
    composed text with nothing sent. The mode transition now returns
    its error through the slash-command contract, so the draft stays in
    the input, nothing is dispatched to the model, and only a
    successful transition clears the input (a trailing prompt still
    ships as the first planning turn on success). The composer toggle
    and `/plan` share this single request/error path.
  * Unsupported-command rejections are mapped to an actionable notice
    ("Plan mode is not supported by this machine's omp-web — upgrade it
    to 0.5.7 or newer") instead of the raw 500 body. Regression tests
    pin the failure contract (error result, no prompt, no success
    message) and the message mapping; both failure shapes — remote 500
    passthrough for `/plan` with trailing text and a toggle click with a
    live draft — were verified in the browser to preserve the composer
    verbatim.

